e importance of family names.","right":"name","misses":2,"students":2,"commonWrongAnswer":"title","commonWrongCount":1},{"where":"english-literature-aqa/macbeth/8","question":"How does Malcolm test Macduff’s loyalty?","right":"He pretends to be worse than Macbeth to see if Macduff will reject a bad king","misses":2,"students":2,"commonWrongAnswer":"He challenges him to a duel","commonWrongCount":1},{"where":"english-literature-aqa/macbeth/1","question":"The witches speak in _____ tetrameter, which contrasts with the iambic pentameter used by other characters.","right":"trochaic","misses":2,"students":2,"commonWrongAnswer":"anapestic","commonWrongCount":1},{"where":"english-literature-aqa/macbeth/8","question":"Malcolm lists the “_____-becoming graces” that define the qualities of a good ruler.","right":"king","misses":2,"students":2,"commonWrongAnswer":"throne","commonWrongCount":2},{"where":"english-literature-aqa/romeo-and-juliet/1","question":"Romeo and Juliet are described as '_____ lovers' in the Prologue, meaning their fate is controlled by the stars.","right":"star-cross'd","misses":2,"students":2,"commonWrongAnswer":"ill-fated","commonWrongCount":2}],"activity":{"this week":0,"last week":0,"this month":25,"over a month":0,"never":0}}